OPlus battery-capacity reporting for crDroid 17.0 / OnePlus sm8750.
Prepared 2026-10-20.

MOTIVATION

Provide manufacturer-aligned battery-health values in Android by using the
existing OPlus capacity correction, rather than deriving the display solely
from raw FCC. The goal is reporting closer to the manufacturer ROM, without
hardcoding a desired percentage.

REFERENCE REPOSITORY, COMMIT AND PUBLIC SOURCE

  kernel/oneplus/sm8750-modules 204b190250343259fc7925c6f50a9365b2bff629 https://github.com/crdroidandroid/android_kernel_oneplus_sm8750-modules branch=17.0

PATCH INVENTORY AND BEHAVIOUR

  crdroid_oplus_battery_capacity.patch
  SHA256: 9e4719bd077826cce32ef9fb44082a25939c06e26abd5f08cd78729acc2e2351

The patch changes oplus/kernel/charger/v2/oplus_chg_gki.c. Its FCC calculation
follows the existing OPlus configfs reporting implementation in the same public
source repository, oplus/kernel/charger/v2/oplus_configfs.c:
  min(raw FCC + FCC coefficient * SOH / 100, design capacity).
The coefficient and SOH are read from the gauge. Missing or invalid metadata
retains raw FCC. The design capacity is read from the gauge with a cached-value
fallback. The intermediate calculation uses 64 bits; mAh-to-uAh conversion is
performed once in each power-supply property.

No gauge state or charging setting is written. The separate UI-SOH model is not
substituted for FCC. No fixed capacity, percentage or device correction value
is introduced. This module does not reproduce a complete manufacturer UI model.

